      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s first post office, opened in 1873, honored William Reason Reagan, a land donor who helped lay out the townsite.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/reagan-tx",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Reagan’s growth began when the Waco and Northwestern Railroad laid tracks through the area in 1873, linking it to regional trade.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
